Hi Sebastian,

Thanks for reaching out! I went through your draft, it seems like you =
were indeed moving towards the same direction.

This is the nature of research, and there is a lot of concurrent work. =
Still, we work on open-ended problems so nothing is yet completely =
final. There are a few topics following this work already. I could guide =
you for the thesis for a possible publication if this sounds =
interesting.

Dropping a few papers to discuss further:

Queen for dynamic static separation (via residuals here): =
https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.04469
MoRGS for motion masking: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.25042
4DGC for Gaussian compression (to optimize storage costs): =
https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.18421

Were you able to run anything regarding Gaussian Splatting (perhaps the =
original repo) so far? Do you have the hardware (GPU) to work on it?

I am blocked by another paper submission until the end of this week, but =
I=E2=80=99d be happy to follow up with you next week. Let me know about =
your availability.

Best,
Idil


